calcite                   https://www.mindat.org/min-859.html
                          Found in most geologic settings and as a
                          later forming replacement mineral in most
                          other environments in one form or another,
                          it is most common as massive material
                          in limestones and marbles. It forms as
                          chemical sedimentary deposits as limestone,
                          can be regionally or contact metamorphosed
                          into marbles and rarely forms igneous
                          rocks (carbonatites). Also is a common
                          gangue mineral in hydrothermal deposits.

                          major:  G01 G03 G05
