halloysite                    source: ?
                             halloysite: Halloysite is found in widely varied environments,
                             including as an alteration of basaltic rocks, in hydrothermally
                             altered fissure deposits in monzonites; it is also derived from
                             feldspars, chlorites, micas, rhyolites, granites, volcanic ash,
                             tuffs and pumices. More rarely found in granitic pegmatites,
                             bauxites or laterites, and in some marine and glacial clays.


hectorite
hedenbergite

hematite                      source: ?
                              hematite: Large ore bodies of hematite
                              are usually of sedimentary origin;
                              also found in high-grade ore bodies
                              in metamorphic rocks due to contact
                              metasomatism, and occasionally as a
                              sublimate on igneous extrusive rocks
                              ("lavas") as a result of volcanic
                              activity. It is also usually the
                              cause of red soils all over the planet.

hematite_smallgrain           G05 G07

